<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Vertex posts higher 96 net profit.</title>
<headline>Czech Vertex posts higher 96 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vertex a.s., a Czech maker of glass fibre products, said on Friday that its net profit in 1996 rose to 200.7 million crowns from a previous 116.8 million the previous year.</p>
<p>It added in a statement that the firm plans to pay a 20 crown per share gross dividend for 1996, unchanged from its dividend for 1995.  </p>
<p>Results for year ending December 31, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit	     200.714    vs     116.820</p>
<p> Operational profit   237.919    vs     212.616</p>
<p>Revenues from sales of products</p>
<p>  and services	1,976.607    vs   1,674.744</p>
<p> Basic capital	1,704.846    vs   1,704.846</p>
<p> Total assets	 3,686.530    vs   3,084.685</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Vertex a.s., the largest Czech glass fibre products maker.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
